SUMMARY:World AIDS Day
DESCRIPTION:Join the LGBTQ+ Culture Center for World AIDS Day\, an evenin
 g of remembrance\, reflection\, and hope featuring keynote speaker Ace Ro
 binson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.\, Director of Sexual &amp\; Gender Minority (Que
 er) Wellness at Duke University.&#160\;      A nationally recognized HIV 
 policy advocate and population health expert\, Ace Robinson has spent mor
 e than two decades advancing health equity and supporting communities dis
 proportionately impacted by HIV. Throughout his career\, he has held lead
 ership roles with organizations including the National Minority AIDS Coun
 cil (NMAC)\, Gay Men's Health Crisis (GMHC)\, the Desmond Tutu Health Fou
 ndation in South Africa\, and the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA
 .&#160\;      In his keynote\,"Willing Our Way to End the HIV Epidemic\,"
  Robinson will explore the progress made in HIV prevention and treatment\
 , the challenges that remain\, and the collective action needed to build 
 a future free from stigma\, discrimination\, and health inequities.&#160\
 ;      Following the keynote\, participants will have an opportunity to g
 ather in community as we honor those lost to HIV/AIDS\, recognize the res
 ilience of people living with HIV\, and recommit ourselves to creating a 
 more just and compassionate future.      HIV &amp\; STI Testing (IU Healt
 h - Positive Link &amp\; Monroe County Health Department) will be provide
 d.  All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, c
 ultural\, and historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana U
 niversity community.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div><p>    Join the LGBTQ+ Culture Center f
 or World AIDS Day\, an evening of remembrance\, reflection\, and hope fea
 turing keynote speaker <strong>Ace Robinson\, M.P.H.\, M.H.L.</strong>\, 
 Director of Sexual &amp\; Gender Minority (Queer) Wellness at Duke Univer
 sity.&#160\;  </p><p>    A nationally recognized HIV policy advocate and 
 population health expert\, Ace Robinson has spent more than two decades a
 dvancing health equity and supporting communities disproportionately impa
 cted by HIV. Throughout his career\, he has held leadership roles with or
 ganizations including the National Minority AIDS Council (NMAC)\, Gay Men
 's Health Crisis (GMHC)\, the Desmond Tutu Health Foundation in South Afr
 ica\, and the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA.&#160\;  </p><p>   
  In his keynote\,<strong>"Willing Our Way to End the HIV Epidemic\,"</str
 ong> Robinson will explore the progress made in HIV prevention and treatm
 ent\, the challenges that remain\, and the collective action needed to bu
 ild a future free from stigma\, discrimination\, and health inequities.&#
 160\;  </p><p>    Following the keynote\, participants will have an oppor
 tunity to gather in community as we honor those lost to HIV/AIDS\, recogn
 ize the resilience of people living with HIV\, and recommit ourselves to 
 creating a more just and compassionate future.  </p><p>    HIV &amp\; STI
  Testing (IU Health - Positive Link &amp\; Monroe County Health Departmen
 t) will be provided.  </p><p><strong>All Indiana University events\, grou
 ps\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, and historical observances wel
 come all members of the Indiana University community.</strong></p></div>
