LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Writing Under Pres
 sure: A Diplomatic & Digital Crisis Simulation
DESCRIPTION:Never Done a Simulation Before? You Belong Here.  You do not 
 need to be a political science expert\, a tech guru\, or a public speaker
  to attend. If you have never done a simulation before\, this is designed
  specifically for you to try something brand new in a zero-pressure envir
 onment.  Got 20 or 30 minutes between classes? Drop in whenever your morn
 ing permits\, grab free snacks and drinks\, and jump right in.  What Actu
 ally Happens in the Room?  Imagine breaking news hits: foreign civil unre
 st erupts\, viral AI fakes flood social media\, and leaked messages throw
  everything into chaos. Top decision-makers at the White House or Google 
 do not have time for a 10-page essay—they need a 4-sentence update righ
 t now. Working alongside a small team\, you will dive into a fast-moving\
 , live-edited scenario where you separate signal from noise\, filter out 
 fake information\, and learn how to draft high-stakes executive briefs in
  real time with guidance from seasoned experts.  Why Show Up?Master the B
 LUF Method: Learn the "Bottom Line Up Front" writing trick that top diplo
 mats\, intelligence analysts\, and Silicon Valley managers use to write e
 mails decision-makers actually read.    The "Cut 30%" Challenge: Learn ho
 w to edit out fluff and sound clear and confident in your everyday writin
 g.    Low Friction: Drop in\, grab food\, work with a small group\, and l
 eave when you need to head to your next class. No prep work or prior read
 ing required.      Target Audience  Open to ALL undergraduate\, Master\, 
 and PhD students across HLS\, Cybersecurity\, Data Science\, Public Polic
 y\, Informatics\, and related majors. Staff and faculty are welcome too!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="12">  Never Done a Si
 mulation Before? You Belong Here.</h4><p data-path-to-node="13">  You do 
 not need to be a political science expert\, a tech guru\, or a public spe
 aker to attend. If you have never done a simulation before\, this is desi
 gned specifically for you to try something brand new in a zero-pressure e
 nvironment.</p><p data-path-to-node="14">  Got 20 or 30 minutes between c
 lasses? Drop in whenever your morning permits\, grab free snacks and drin
 ks\, and jump right in.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="15">  What Actually Hap
 pens in the Room?</h4><p data-path-to-node="16">  Imagine breaking news h
 its: foreign civil unrest erupts\, viral AI fakes flood social media\, an
 d leaked messages throw everything into chaos. Top decision-makers at the
  White House or Google do not have time for a 10-page essay—they need a
  4-sentence update right now. Working alongside a small team\, you will d
 ive into a fast-moving\, live-edited scenario where you separate signal f
 rom noise\, filter out fake information\, and learn how to draft high-sta
 kes executive briefs in real time with guidance from seasoned experts.</p
 ><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Why Show Up?</h4><ul data-path-to-node="18"
 ><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0"
  data-index-in-node="0">Master the BLUF Method:</strong> Learn the "Botto
 m Line Up Front" writing trick that top diplomats\, intelligence analysts
 \, and Silicon Valley managers use to write emails decision-makers actual
 ly read.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,1\,0"><strong data-pat
 h-to-node="18\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="0">The "Cut 30%" Challenge:</str
 ong> Learn how to edit out fluff and sound clear and confident in your ev
 eryday writing.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,2\,0"><strong d
 ata-path-to-node="18\,2\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Low Friction:</strong>
  Drop in\, grab food\, work with a small group\, and leave when you need 
 to head to your next class. No prep work or prior reading required.    </
 p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="20">  Target Audience</h3><p data-path
 -to-node="21">  Open to ALL undergraduate\, Master\, and PhD students acr
 oss HLS\, Cybersecurity\, Data Science\, Public Policy\, Informatics\, an
 d related majors. Staff and faculty are welcome too!</p>
